    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green: **57 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## What changed\n\n`AuditOwnerCreated.service` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`) now logs `membershipNumber` in addition to the fields it already emitted (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel`).\n\nKey detail: `membershipLevel` is a `static` method on `OwnerMapper`, but `membershipNumber` is a `default` (instance) method. So I injected the `OwnerMapper` bean as a function parameter \u2014 the same way sibling functions like `RespondWithOwnerCreated` receive it \u2014 and derived the number via `ownerMapper.membershipNumber(owner)` rather than duplicating the format logic. The observed audit line confirms it:\n\n```\nAUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-08-17 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26\n```",
